{"5324510":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"The Crane Files: A Detective Mystery","steam_appid":5324510,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"detailed_description":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Ten murders. A paper crane at every scene.<\/h2><strong>The Crane Files<\/strong> is a murder mystery deduction game. Investigate ten hand-built 3D crime scenes, question the suspects, and work out exactly what happened: who did it, how, why and when. Nothing is handed to you, and every answer needs evidence.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >How it plays<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Investigate<\/strong> every scene. Rotate and zoom each room and examine every object, body and document.<br><\/li><li><strong>Question<\/strong> the suspects. Everyone has a story, and most of them are hiding something.<br><\/li><li><strong>Collect<\/strong> words from clues and statements: names, times, weapons, motives.<br><\/li><li><strong>Deduce<\/strong> by filling in the blanks. Get close and the game lets you know, but never which blank is wrong.<\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Ten cases, each with a new twist<\/h2>A locked study. A kitchen alibi and a two-room timeline. Anonymous passengers on the last train. A holiday party where everyone is lying. A garden to compare before and after. Two crimes with two culprits. A cabin full of motives. A night market with eight suspects. A castle gala with two killers working together. And a final case that ties every file together, and unmasks whoever has been leaving the cranes.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>10 handcrafted cases, about 2 to 3 hours of play<br><\/li><li>135 blanks to fill, every one backed by evidence<br><\/li><li>Optional hints that point you at the next wrong or empty blank without giving the answer<br><\/li><li>A detective's notebook that records everything you find<br><\/li><li>Stylised 3D scenes and an original soundtrack<br><\/li><li>No combat, no timers. Play at your own pace<br><\/li><li>Progress saves automatically<\/li><\/ul><br><strong>Content note:<\/strong> murder themes throughout. The scenes are stylised, with no blood or gore. The game is in English.","about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Ten murders. A paper crane at every scene.<\/h2><strong>The Crane Files<\/strong> is a murder mystery deduction game. Investigate ten hand-built 3D crime scenes, question the suspects, and work out exactly what happened: who did it, how, why and when. Nothing is handed to you, and every answer needs evidence.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >How it plays<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Investigate<\/strong> every scene. Rotate and zoom each room and examine every object, body and document.<br><\/li><li><strong>Question<\/strong> the suspects. Everyone has a story, and most of them are hiding something.<br><\/li><li><strong>Collect<\/strong> words from clues and statements: names, times, weapons, motives.<br><\/li><li><strong>Deduce<\/strong> by filling in the blanks. Get close and the game lets you know, but never which blank is wrong.<\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Ten cases, each with a new twist<\/h2>A locked study. A kitchen alibi and a two-room timeline. Anonymous passengers on the last train. A holiday party where everyone is lying. A garden to compare before and after. Two crimes with two culprits. A cabin full of motives. A night market with eight suspects. A castle gala with two killers working together. And a final case that ties every file together, and unmasks whoever has been leaving the cranes.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>10 handcrafted cases, about 2 to 3 hours of play<br><\/li><li>135 blanks to fill, every one backed by evidence<br><\/li><li>Optional hints that point you at the next wrong or empty blank without giving the answer<br><\/li><li>A detective's notebook that records everything you find<br><\/li><li>Stylised 3D scenes and an original soundtrack<br><\/li><li>No combat, no timers. Play at your own pace<br><\/li><li>Progress saves automatically<\/li><\/ul><br><strong>Content note:<\/strong> murder themes throughout. The scenes are stylised, with no blood or gore. The game is in English.","short_description":"A murder mystery deduction game. Investigate ten 3D crime scenes, question the suspects, collect clues as words, then fill in exactly what happened. Every answer needs evidence. And someone leaves a paper crane at every scene.","supported_languages":"English","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5324510\/247fad1e685e4f6ab2b9ceb440966584d678db26\/header.jpg?t=1793738255","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5324510\/f5d6c00bf393a8304bd6229122fc75e5b741f66d\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793738255","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5324510\/f5d6c00bf393a8304bd6229122fc75e5b741f66d\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793738255","website":null,"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 10 64-bit<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Dual-core 2.0 GHz<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 4 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Vulkan 1.0 compatible, 1 GB VRAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 300 MB available space<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<\/li><\/ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> macOS 10.15 or later<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Apple Silicon or Intel (universal build)<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 4 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Metal-capable GPU<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 300 MB available space<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/s